# Sanjeevani patch template: loop runs one iteration too many.

name: off-by-one loop bound
cwe: CWE-193 off-by-one error

# A for-loop whose continuation test is <= against a limit. In decompiled C
# Ghidra renders these as local_XX names, so match generic identifiers.
detect: for\s*\([^;]*;\s*\w+\s*<=\s*\w+\s*;

find: (for\s*\([^;]*;\s*\w+\s*)<=(\s*\w+\s*;)
replace: \1<\2

explain: an array of N elements has valid indices 0 to N-1. A loop written with
 i <= N runs N+1 times and writes one element past the end. Changing <= to <
 is the whole fix.

caveat: only correct when the bound is the element COUNT. If the bound is
 already the last valid index, <= was right and this would drop the final
 element - which the equivalence proof would catch.
